        <p>
          Your data trains their models.
          Your access disappears when they change their pricing.
        </p>
        <div class="problem-divider"></div>
        <p class="problem-turn">
          Netclaw runs on <em>your</em> hardware, connects to <em>your</em> channels, and stays on &mdash;
          24/7, no exceptions. It handles the stuff you keep putting off: triaging alerts,
          posting updates, running the checks nobody remembers to run.
        </p>
